<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21265" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īăpĕtus</span></b> ,
		i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰαπετός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Titan</i>, <i>son of Uranos and
				Gœa</i>, <i>the father of Atlas</i>,
				<i>Prometheus</i>, <i>and
			Epimetheus</i>, Hyg. F. praef.; 54; 142; 144; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1,
				279</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lact. 2, 10, 7 sq.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">satus Iapeto,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Prometheus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 82</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">called also Iapeti genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 3, 27</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īăpĕtīŏnĭdes</span></b> ,
				ae, m., <i>a male
				descendant of Iapetus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atlas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 632</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fratres gemini,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Prometheus and Epimetneus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Eutr. 2, 49</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
